<title>UK: RESEARCH ALERT-Lehman says GEC undervalued.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT-Lehman says GEC undervalued.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brokerage Lehman Brothers said General Electric Co Plc shares were undervalued on Monday, and put a 1997 target on the share price of 400p.</p>
<p>By 1321 GMT, the shares were up 1-1/2p to 335-1/2.</p>
<p>Lehman analyst Charles Armitage said the shares were &quot;unfairly hit&quot; by worries about possible UK government defence cuts and by the Socialist victory in France.</p>
<p>&quot;GEC's existing business is undervalued,&quot; Armitage said. &quot;They're looking further than Europe, they're looking globally.&quot;</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 5106</p>
